  "text_md": "MRCPUK\n\n![](<b773892dc3e755672b9e085e9eeb8ad18690_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\n# SCE in Nephrology Blueprint    \n\nCandidates are tested on a wide range of common and important disorders as set\n\n# MRCP(UK) Central Office\n\n11 St Andrews Place Regent’s Park London NW1 4LE\n\nTel: +44 (0)20 3075 1515\n\nwww.mrcpuk.org\n\nThe composition of the paper is as follows:  \n\nNumber of questions*\n\nTopic\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>    Glomerulonephritis, tubulointerstitial (incl. vasculitis, anti-GBM  </th>\n    <th>Number of questions* 30</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Acute kidney injury, acute therapy, disorders of fluid,</td>\n    <td>26</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Chronic kidney disease, haematuria; proteinuria</td>\n    <td>24</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>  Renal bone disease, renal  </td>\n    <td>12</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Cardiovascular disease, renovascular disease and</td>\n    <td>20</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>  Urological presentations stone disease, urinary tract</td>\n    <td>14</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>and obstruction     Inherited and rarer diseases</td>\n    <td>14</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>  Peritoneal dialysis  </td>\n    <td>      8</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>  Haemodialysis    </td>\n    <td>      14</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Renal transplantation  </td>\n    <td>      14</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Other^</td>\n    <td>24</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\n200\n\n# Total\n\n  The questions in each category are distributed across both papers  \n\n*This should be taken as an indication of the likely number of questions – the actual number may vary.  \n\n‘Other’ includes the following topics:\n\nTherapeutics & safe prescribing\n\nRenal disorders in pregnancy\n\nInfection in the renal patient\n\nActive supportive (non-dialysis) care\n\nNutrition\n\ncal procedures\n\nSexual health\n\nAdult-paediatric interface\n\nEnd-of-life care MP\n\nRCPE\n\nRoyal College of\n\n![](<b773892dc3e755672b9e085e9eeb8ad18690_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\nPhysicians of Edinburgh\n\n![](<b773892dc3e755672b9e085e9eeb8ad18690_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile3.png>)\n\nROYAL COLLEGE OF\n\n![](<b773892dc3e755672b9e085e9eeb8ad18690_pg1_pg1_images/imageFile4.png>)\n\nRoyal College\n\nof Physicians\n\n",
